{
  "version": 1,
  "exactInitialPilotCandidate": {
    "status": "candidate",
    "disposition": "2026-11-27 final D2 candidate disposition: the one-shot read-this-page pilot requires one initial exact document. Only %20 (an escaped space) is permitted among percent sequences; this supersedes both the earlier wider-uppercase-escape and no-percent proposals. Never obtain origin authority first, silently widen scope or auto-expand. Existing explicit origin approval is separate released behavior, not a substitute for this pilot. Candidate rows do not prove redirect, committed document or generation (broker R12), runtime support or release readiness.",
    "fixtureMapping": "In CI only, map billing.example.test:8443 to a synthetic loopback HTTPS server in the disposable environment. Test the named HTTPS URL, not an IP-literal bypass.",
    "unsupportedLiteral": {
      "message": "URL not supported in this pilot",
      "reviewCommandCount": 0,
      "adapterCalls": 0,
      "fallback": false
    },
    "contexts": {
      "general": "Existing catalog-aware v1 leaseScope reference over the complete typed allow array and raw candidate; not a universal ingress policy. consumerOverrides map named seam exceptions. Go enforces 2048 bytes and runs its protected checks, kernel rule is generic up to 8192 without a protected-host policy. BIOS must independently enforce the pilot protected deny list. WASI proves emitted/absent typed request and command, not authority.",
      "pilot": "Single initial typed exact rule, byte-identical canonical HTTPS href at intake and at externally supplied goto. A true means syntactic eligibility, not authority. Reject parent, query and fragment even when empty. ASCII DNS A-label multi-label host, no trailing dot, IP/numeric alias, localhost or single-label. Canonical non-default port allowed. Path is root or slash-delimited nonempty ASCII unreserved segments, optional trailing slash, no dot/dotdot, and exactly one permitted escape: uppercase %20 for space. No literal space, percent decoding, second decoding or rewriting: pass the accepted ASCII spelling unchanged. All other encodings, including reserved characters and UTF-8, are denied in this pilot (future support undecided). A valid ACE label must decode to non-ASCII and round-trip to identical lowercase ASCII via an existing IDNA validator. A consumer lacking such validation must deny every xn-- host, report this limitation and not count the valid ACE row as passed. Cap 2048 UTF-8 bytes before/after serialization. Never widen/fallback/retry. False pilot columns for a valid origin are not a legacy-origin refusal. Root and a terminal slash are distinct; nonterminal empty path segments are forbidden. Admission assumes other checks such as the 900s pilot term and holder are already satisfied. In pilot syntax failures, no emitted command and no adapter call; never infer that for a valid independent legacy origin.",
      "grantEcho": "Given independently valid signed grant and bound context, compare immutable offerAllow and grantAllow cardinality, canonical kind and URL byte-for-byte. sameTypedSingleRule tests identity even when not eligible for this pilot; additionally require valid D2 offer for pilotGrantAccepted. False means zero data OPENs and zero browser dispatch (not zero request control OPENs). Kill kind-only mutant at tuple-comparison unit seam; an earlier kind/prefix rejection must not be reported as that mutant kill.",
      "ownerReview": "Compare proven requests to the owner-selected holder, rule tuple and duration using the actual emitted command in POSIX shell argv only; single-quote each accepted exact URL atom and preserve literal %20 bytes. This is not a Windows cmd/batch rendering guarantee. Negative D2 input must not produce an owner line. PTY compatibility is separate from signing and production release evidence. offer is the proven pending broker request. owner is the decoded owner review line. expectedLine names the owner-side test input, and the matching ownerReview rows also specify exact client output. Generic duration-format controls are not BIOS pilot eligibility. A mismatched line in a negative case is not output expected from a legitimate producer.",
      "finalDocument": "unverified-R12: no row asserts the final committed URL, generation or disclosure after redirect. Broker R12 owns that verification."
    },
    "freeze": "Candidate data only. Record acceptance separately against the unchanged digest after WASI, kernel, BIOS and Go have each run and acknowledged these exact bytes in CI and the guard owner accepts. A discrepancy is a named finding, not an expected-pass waiver. No authority, dispatch, final-document identity, deployment or release follows from this digest."
  },
